# Copy to `.env.local` for local Vite dev (see https://vitejs.dev/guide/env-and-mode).
# `.env.local` is gitignored — never commit it. Only this file belongs in version control.
#
# Client-safe (Vite `VITE_*` prefix — bundled into the browser build):
#   - Supabase project URL + publishable/anon key (public by design)
#   - Meta pixel ID
#
# Server-only (NEVER put in `.env.local` or any `VITE_*` variable):
#   - Twilio, Meta CAPI, Gemini, dev bypass, dispatch — set via `supabase secrets set`
#   - See "Supabase Edge Function Secrets" below

# ═══ Supabase (client — safe to expose in frontend) ═══
VITE_SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID="your-project-id"
VITE_SUPABASE_URL="https://your-project.supabase.co"
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="your-public-anon-key"
# Optional alias; `src/integrations/supabase/client.ts` accepts either key name.
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY="your-public-anon-key"

# ═══ Dev Bypass (DEV ONLY — NO BUILD-TIME SECRET) ═══
# The client-side dev bypass is no longer read from the build env.
# It is stored in browser localStorage at runtime via window.prompt:
#   - First DEV-only action prompts: "Enter DEV_BYPASS_SECRET (cancel to use normal OTP flow):"
#   - Value persists in localStorage.wm_dev_secret
#   - To clear: localStorage.removeItem('wm_dev_secret') in DevTools
# Implementation: src/lib/devSecret.ts
#
# Server enforcement (the only real boundary) lives in DEV_BYPASS_SECRET
# (Supabase secrets) — used by supabase/functions/dev-report-unlock and
# supabase/functions/_shared/adminAuth.ts. Rotating the server secret
# instantly invalidates every browser's stored value.

# ═══ Facebook / Meta (client pixel ID only) ═══
VITE_META_PIXEL_ID="your-pixel-id"

# ═══ Dark V2 homepage report renderer ═══
# false — existing Classic TruthReportClassic post-scan renderer (default).
# true  — Dark V2 partial/full report UI on the homepage scan funnel.
# Vite env vars are evaluated at dev-server/build startup; restart `npm run dev`
# after changing this in `.env.local`, and rebuild for production deployment.
VITE_ENABLE_DARK_V2_HOMEPAGE=false

# ═══ Supabase Edge Function Secrets (set via supabase secrets set) ═══
# Do not duplicate these in `.env.local`. Names must match what edge functions read.
#
# Dev bypass for _shared/adminAuth.ts and dev-report-unlock.
# MUST remain unset or "false" in production. Setting to "true"
# enables the x-dev-secret header to grant super_admin access.
# DEV_BYPASS_ENABLED=false
# DEV_BYPASS_SECRET=your-secret-here
#
# Meta Conversions API (server — `capi-event` edge function)
# META_PIXEL_ID=your-pixel-id
# META_CAPI_TOKEN=your-conversions-api-access-token
#
# Twilio Verify (`send-otp`, `verify-otp`)
# TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=your-twilio-sid
# TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=your-twilio-auth-token
# TWILIO_VERIFY_SERVICE_SID=your-verify-service-sid
#
# Scanner / AI (`scan-quote` expects exact name GEMINI_API_KEY)
# GEMINI_API_KEY=your-gemini-api-key
# GEMINI_SCAN_MODEL=gemini-3.1-flash-lite-preview
#
# Lead dispatch webhook
# DISPATCH_LEAD_SECRET=your-dispatch-secret
